{
  "set": "reputation-settlement-semantics-v0.4",
  "spec": "DACS-5 v0.4 §10.5.1 RSV-1..RSV-4; settlement-verified types; consumes existing DACS-4 rules",
  "decisionModel": "accept admits the job; reject and indeterminate exclude it without fault; a legacy agreement with a historical LAA pass is current-ineligible and excluded from every current numerator, denominator, rating, volume, bundleCount and bundleRefs",
  "inputModel": "one authoritative bundle projection after cross-copy settlementEvidence reference-multiset agreement; every case uses an authenticated Agreement price of 5 DEM; evidencePhase defaults to the DACS-4 §9.7 PaymentPhaseType pay-dem for non-empty inputs, and only exact membership in that closed type can establish payment volume; evidence outcome defaults to success; authorityDisposition is the independent transaction/authority resolution result; mismatch is evaluated only when authorityDisposition is verified and names the sole semantic contradiction; mismatchIndex selects the zero-based member when present; null then means all semantic checks match; legacyAgreement marks a successful payment citing legacy AgreementDocument and laa carries its full DACS-4 LAA-1..LAA-7 admission input, evaluated by the shared oracle (a historical pass is current-ineligible; a missing, malformed, or unknown laa input is non-authorizing and rejected, never default-accepted)",
  "hash": "78c1e0728b118374973dcad7b803bd9c1243873b7675ed9d61dd4d9930bc7571",
